pr.body:
Loading the array returned by `.root().get()` makes ordinary selectors return no matches, even though the document still contains the elements. This affects the documented node-array input to `load()`.

The parser recognizes a Document passed directly but wraps `[Document]` in a second root. Selector traversal then skips that nested document. Reuse the document for a singleton Document array, matching the existing direct-document behavior and preserving its DOM links. Other node arrays keep their current handling.

```js
import { load } from 'cheerio';

const original = load('<html><body><p>Hello</p></body></html>');
const $ = load(original.root().get());
console.log(JSON.stringify([$('html').length, $('p').text()]));
```

Before: `[0, ""]`. After: `[1, "Hello"]`.

Fixes #4000.


